{
  "$comment": "Page contracts, version 3 (docs/design/target-state.md v2.1). This file measures rendered STRINGS — headings, tabs, tiles, columns, chips, buttons, summaries, links and prose budgets — for the surfaces as currently built. It is not a visual-anatomy authority and never was: composition, widths, density, placement, disclosure and responsive behaviour for Home, Connect, Plan and MFA Readiness belong to the approved packs in docs/design/approved/ (manifest.json). A restoration pack (030+) may change a surface's layout without contradicting this file, and updates an allow list here only when the strings the surface renders change. One entry per surface the UI inventory walks. Every rendered heading, tab, tile, column, chip, button, summary and link on a built surface must match an entry in its allow list (exact string, or a regular expression when prefixed re:). Page-level prose (outside repeaters) must fit the budget. Claude Code never edits this file: a violation is fixed by removing what violates it, or reported for review with the case. `status` is `built` for a surface that is measured; a status of the form `planned:<prompt>` names the prompt that builds the surface and flips it to `built` — a surface that is not `built` is not measured. `enforceAll` is true: any inventory surface without a contract fails, so a deleted surface (the Recovery card) fails the build if it still renders. Controls (buttons, links, chips) inside a repeater are items and are measured under `rows`, not against the surface's allow lists. An element matching `.step-title` is reported as `title` and measured against rules.stepTitleMaxWords, never as a heading. A surface may override the row budget with `rowBudget`. `forbid` and `forbidEverywhere` entries are case-sensitive substrings.",
